                "text": "**Analyzing Block Structure**\n\nI'm currently focused on dissecting the 9x9 grid's structure. It's naturally broken down into nine 3x3 blocks, which is where my thought process is focused. I am now trying to formulate a clear pattern to represent the block positions. Specifically, I'm thinking about how to represent the blocks using indices.\n\n\n**Discovering Masking Patterns**\n\nI've made a significant leap. The 3x3 block pattern acts as a binary mask, dictating which other blocks contain the same internal 3x3 pattern. It is a fractal, similar to a Kronecker product, where the mask defines the \"active\" blocks. For instance, in Train 1, a specific pattern in block (1,1) defines which other blocks will hold the pattern in a specific way. The 3x3 pattern inside (1,1) serves as a mask. This is reinforced by considering Train 2.\n\n\n",
